# netsurf: a flex or grid container's own class or style restyles it alone (patch 372)
# Generated 2026-11-06
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 371)
#
# The r96 census, after 371 cleared "page has frames": rte's five style
# changes declined on "class change on an element with a non-inline,
# non-block box". A temporary trace showed all five were slick carousel
# tracks -- <div class="slick-track" style="opacity:1;width:59616px;
# transform:translate(...)">, BOX_FLEX in a block, 75-335 boxes, 4 of 5
# with no object -- whose style slick writes on every slide. Each write
# was a full box-tree rebuild: 107 ms on a 2500-paragraph sim page.
#
#  - html.c: html_rl_flex_restyle(). A class or style change on an
#    element whose own box is BOX_FLEX or BOX_GRID builds the container
#    again on its own, as patch 369 builds a cell's table: the old box
#    freed, box_build_element cascading the container and its items
#    afresh from the DOM (descendant selectors and inheritance reach the
#    items), the new box linked where the old one was, normalised, and the
#    page laid out whole. display:none is a removal; a container that
#    became a block is normalised as one.
#  - Declined: a container holding objects, controls or frames (others
#    point at those boxes; HTML_RL_FRAME of 371); one not directly in a
#    block, cell, flex or grid box (a float's or an inline's); a sibling
#    selector the class can move (patch 186); counters in page CSS. One
#    that became inline-level (inline-flex) after the build is handed to
#    the full reconvert, as 369 does.
#  - box_normalise.c/h: box_normalise_flex_ext(), box_normalise_flex for
#    one container (as 369's box_normalise_table_ext).
#
# Result on the sim page: the track's style 107 -> 19 ms; a flex class
# 107 -> 19 ms; a grid class 18 ms.
#
